config ETC_APP_LTE_SYNC_NACK_THRESHOLD
	int "Unacknowledged readings above which a LoRa logger also uploads over LTE"
	default 3
	help
	  FW-788. A LoRa logger with strictly more than this many unacknowledged
	  readings at a transmit interval brings up LTE in addition to its normal
	  LoRa attempt. Set very large to disable the behaviour.

config ETC_APP_LTE_SYNC_BACKOFF_MULTIPLE
	int "Minimum spacing between LTE bring-ups, in transmit intervals"
	default 4
	help
	  FW-789 floor. Opportunistic LTE bring-ups are attempted at most once per
	  this many tx intervals (default 4 x 900 s = 1 h).

config ETC_APP_LTE_SYNC_BACKOFF_MAX_S
	int "Ceiling for the exponential LTE backoff, in seconds"
	default 86400
	help
	  FW-789 ceiling. After consecutive failed bring-ups the spacing doubles
	  from the floor but never exceeds this (default once per day).
